@startuml http_session_event_stream
title CampusClaw Session Event Direct POST Stream

' Source evidence (pi-mono 086c32e74530564922d011ade23ff582c9d63116):
' packages/agent/src/types.ts, AgentEvent, lines 430-443
' packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts, emitToolExecutionEnd and emitToolResultMessage,
' lines 767-795
' packages/coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts, _handleAgentEvent, lines 781-806
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 1f801dbb82bdda30478e3354e685e3153b179a0c):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventController.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventService.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/agent/RuntimeAgentPromptLoader.java.
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 304eda06ff603fc9b6bbcaad0c296cc151a7defb):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/vo/UserEventRequestVO.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEntryCodec.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java.
' Observed behavior: current Java request, history, and SSE payload fields are snake_case.
' Observed behavior: both pi baselines emit message start, update, and end events around
' one active in-memory execution. The Java HTTP handler already returns SSE from POST.
' Observed behavior: the implemented API persists MessageEntry records and has no public run ID.
' Java divergence: unlike the old baseline, client disconnect only detaches the bounded subscriber.
' Architecture change: a disconnected client does not abort accepted execution; GET Session Events is
' the recovery source, and replaying the side-effecting POST is forbidden.
' Design reason: preserve direct streaming while separating transient message and tool
' execution progress from authoritative User, Assistant, and ToolResult entries.
' Observed behavior: internal thinking start, delta, and end events exist, but RuntimeEventProjector
' emits text deltas only and RuntimeEntryCodec currently excludes ThinkingContent from the public contract.
' Architecture change: the target contract projects thinking events only when the accepted execution
' snapshots thinking true; assistant.thinking.completed becomes a durable recoverable entry.
' Architecture change: target request and SSE data fields use lowerCamelCase; event names remain unchanged.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  ActorBorderColor #475569
  ActorFontColor #0F172A
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
  GroupBorderColor #64748B
  GroupFontColor #334155
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7ED
  BorderColor #C2410C
  FontColor #7C2D12
}

actor Caller
participant "Session Event\nAPI" as API
database "Runtime Session\nStore" as Store
participant "Prompt\nLoader" as Prompt
participant "Model\nManager" as Manager
participant AgentSession

Caller -> API : POST /sessions/{sessionId}/events\ncontext headers and message or fileIds JSON
API -> API : do not validate integration credentials
API -> API : validate sessionId and strict request body
API -> Store : load live Session
Store --> API : current model, thinking, and execution state

alt another execution is active
  API --> Caller : 409 SESSION_BUSY\nJSON error without result
else Session is idle
  API -> Prompt : append ordered fileIds as fixed text block
  Prompt --> API : user prompt
  API -> Manager : resolve current model and input policy
  Manager --> API : authoritative model descriptor and limits
  API -> Store : persist User MessageEntry and mark active execution
  Store --> API : user entryId and entrySeq
  API --> Caller : 200 text/event-stream
  API --> Caller : user.message\nentryId and entrySeq
  API -> AgentSession : prompt(user prompt)

  alt execution completes
    loop each Assistant MessageEntry
      AgentSession --> API : message_start
      API --> Caller : assistant.message.started\nentryId, no entrySeq
      loop provider increments
        AgentSession --> API : message_update
        API --> Caller : assistant.message.delta\nentryId and typed delta
      end
      opt execution snapshot thinking is true
        AgentSession --> API : thinking_start
        API --> Caller : assistant.thinking.started\nassistantEntryId and contentIndex
        loop provider thinking increments
          AgentSession --> API : thinking_delta
          API --> Caller : assistant.thinking.delta\ntemporary thinking text
        end
        AgentSession --> API : thinking_end with complete thinking content
        API -> Store : persist complete ThinkingContent entry
        Store --> API : thinking entryId and entrySeq
        API --> Caller : assistant.thinking.completed\ncomplete thinking content and entrySeq
      end
      AgentSession --> API : message_end with complete message
      API -> Store : persist complete Assistant MessageEntry
      Store --> API : entrySeq
      API --> Caller : assistant.message.completed\ncomplete message and entrySeq
      opt tool calls require another model turn
        AgentSession --> API : tool_execution_start
        API --> Caller : tool.execution.started\ntoolCallId and toolName
        AgentSession --> API : tool_execution_end
        API --> Caller : tool.execution.completed\ntoolCallId, toolName, isError
        AgentSession --> API : ToolResult message_start and message_end
        API -> Store : persist complete ToolResultEntry
        Store --> API : tool result entryId and entrySeq
        API --> Caller : tool.result\ncomplete result and entrySeq
      end
    end

    AgentSession --> API : agent_end
    API -> Store : clear active execution and persist final entries
    API --> Caller : session.status.idle
    API --> Caller : stream.end\nreason completed
  else execution fails after stream start
    AgentSession --> API : execution failure
    API -> Store : retain completed entries and clear active execution
    API --> Caller : stream.error\nSESSION_EXECUTION_FAILED and localized message
    API -> API : close stream without stream.end
  end
end

note over API,Caller
Message previews and tool execution events are transient.
User, completed Assistant, and ToolResult entries are authoritative.
Completed Thinking entries are authoritative when the execution
snapshot has thinking true; thinking started and delta are transient.
Session idle and stream end are non-history control events.
Stream error is a terminal non-history event and closes the response.
end note

note over Caller,Store
This POST has no application idempotency key.
After disconnect, do not replay it automatically; call GET Session Events.
The accepted execution continues without the HTTP client.
end note
@enduml

@startuml http_session_event_list
title CampusClaw Session Event List Pagination

' Source evidence (pi-mono 086c32e74530564922d011ade23ff582c9d63116):
' packages/coding-agent/src/core/session-manager.ts, SessionEntry, lines 46-156
' packages/coding-agent/src/core/session-manager.ts, append methods, lines 1057-1149
' packages/coding-agent/src/core/session-manager.ts, getBranch and getEntries, lines 1260-1303
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 8691e8800f05f28afe22499050c29220ef5b7475):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventCursorCodec.java.
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 304eda06ff603fc9b6bbcaad0c296cc151a7defb):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/vo/EventPageResponseVO.java.
' Observed behavior: current Java exposes next_page while the target field is nextPage.
' Observed behavior: pi stores append-only entries linked by id and parentId, and its active
' branch is the path from the selected leaf to the root.
' Java divergence: the old Java baseline scanned JSONL linearly; the implemented repository
' now reads the current branch through parentId and entrySeq.
' External reference (Anthropic Managed Agents docs checked 2026-08-17):
' GET /v1/sessions/{session_id}/events uses opaque page and next_page pagination.
' Observed behavior: entrySeq, opaque pages, ResultBean paging, and the GET endpoint
' exist in the implementation commit but not in the original pi source baselines.
' Java divergence: current RuntimeEntryCodec excludes ThinkingContent from public history.
' Architecture change: target GET visibility depends on the current Session thinking value.
' Design reason: align the public pagination boundary with Anthropic and intentionally
' avoid a fixed snapshot watermark or an afterEntrySeq query while binding the cursor
' to the thinking visibility state used to construct the page.
' Architecture change: CampusClaw target path and payload fields use lowerCamelCase.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  ActorBorderColor #475569
  ActorFontColor #0F172A
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
  GroupBorderColor #64748B
  GroupFontColor #334155
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7ED
  BorderColor #C2410C
  FontColor #7C2D12
}

actor Caller
participant "Session Events\nAPI" as API
database "Runtime Session\nStore" as Store
participant "Page Cursor\nCodec" as Cursor
participant ResultBeanAdapter

alt first page
  Caller -> API : GET /sessions/{sessionId}/events\ncontext headers, limit, no page
  API -> API : do not validate integration credentials
  API -> API : validate sessionId and limit
  API -> Store : read current Session thinking\nand first current-branch entries
  Store --> API : thinking state and persisted entries
  alt current Session thinking is true
    API -> API : include assistant.thinking.completed
  else current Session thinking is false
    API -> API : filter assistant.thinking.completed
  end
  API -> Cursor : encode session, thinking state,\nexpiry, and next position
  Cursor --> API : nextPage or null
else next page
  Caller -> API : GET /sessions/{sessionId}/events\ncontext headers and previous nextPage
  API -> API : do not validate integration credentials
  API -> Cursor : verify and decode opaque page
  Cursor --> API : bound session, thinking state,\nexpiry, and next position
  API -> Store : read current Session thinking
  Store --> API : current thinking state
  break current thinking differs from cursor state
    API --> Caller : 400 INVALID_EVENT_LIST_QUERY\nrestart from the first page
  end
  API -> Store : read after next position and apply\nthe current thinking visibility rule
  Store --> API : eligible persisted entries, including\nlater appends after the cursor
  API -> Cursor : encode current thinking state\nand next position if more remain
  Cursor --> API : nextPage or null
end

API -> ResultBeanAdapter : normal(SessionEventListResponseVO)
ResultBeanAdapter --> API : resCode, resMsg, result
API --> Caller : 200 OK\nevents and nextPage

note over API,Store
Committed user.message, assistant.message.completed, and tool.result
entries on the current branch are always eligible.
assistant.thinking.completed is eligible only when the current
Session thinking value is true. Disabling hides stored thinking
without deleting it; re-enabling can reveal it again.
Items are sorted by entrySeq ascending.
There is no fixed snapshot watermark. Later persisted
entries may become eligible on a subsequent page.
end note

note over API,Cursor
nextPage null means no more persisted events at response time.
It does not mean the Session cannot append future events.
An invalid or expired page returns 400 INVALID_EVENT_LIST_QUERY.
Changing Session thinking also invalidates an old page because
the page is bound to the previous visibility state.
end note
@enduml
